From 939790f7da127484914e7da8e90f49a2452d8638 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Denguinho <k@local>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:38:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: claim verify batches of 2 for the inline-dequant FA
 kernel

GGML_CUDA_FATTN_MMA_Q becomes the smallest Q->ne[1] the inline-dequant MMA path
claims rather than an opaque mode number, and its default moves from 3 to 2.

Measured at kv=54016, q4_0, per FA op: nb=2 goes 484.4 -> 181.5 us, because the
GQA vector kernel re-streams the whole cache once per token while the MMA kernel
reads it once. A draft length of 1 is routine under --spec-draft-p-min 0.3, so
nb=2 is a common verify batch and leaving it on the vector kernel costs 4.85 ms
per step at depth.

nb=1 stays on the vector kernel: there the MMA path measures 300.5 us against
271.0, i.e. 10% slower, because the inline dequant costs more than the vector
kernel's single-column deficit. Patch 0003 is not subsumed.

Batches above 16 (prefill) keep the F16 scratch path: the inline dequant runs once per Q tile, so pp512 measured -3.6%/-3.8% at 32k/64k depth with the path claimed. 16 keeps the same tile count as the largest measured win (batch 9, 2.51x); the exact crossover between 16 and 512 is unmeasured.
